### Limitations the authors admit
- 2016ApJ...823L..18H: Thermal vs non-thermal desorption contributions not constrained; narrow optically thick dust rings need higher resolution
- 2016A&A...587A..91B: Uniform single-component LTE model cannot fit very optically thick lines; formal temperature errors unreliable
- 2019A&A...624A.125M: Fractionation not constrained; source size and Tex assumed; 13CO moderately optically thick; missing short spacings
- 2019A&A...632A..19T: CH3OD partition function uncertain, causing large differences in column densities; possible non-LTE effects
- 2013ApJ...774...16R: Models are degenerate, not unique or optimal; systematic residuals at large radii
- 2013ApJ...774...16R: Band 7 sky frequency in SV measurement set incorrect
- 2025A&A...699A.382M: Field of view truncates the outflow; velocity resolution comparable to gradients; expansion velocity poorly constrained
- 2015ApJ...813L..19J: Gaussian fit underestimates the actual disk size
- 2024ApJ...965..147B: Models do not fully match observations; CO enrichment only 50 vs 20
- 2017A&A...597A..99W: Wind model made for AGB stars and assumes constant isotropic mass loss; only order-of-magnitude estimate
- 2017A&A...597A..99W: ISM emission and filtering of extended emission (>30'') cause contamination and negative artefacts
- 2020ApJ...898...97B: C18O optical depth is a major uncertainty; rare isotopologue needed
- 2020ApJ...898...97B: Small sample: two Class 0 and three Class I sources
- 2020ApJ...898...97B: Resolution too low to identify Keplerian disks
- 2019Icar..319..417T: Large beams average latitudes; HC3N optically thick at poles; low sensitivity above ~400 km
- 2015ApJ...801...63M: Error maps too optimistic; negative bowl from missing short spacings; region 6 fluxes highly uncertain due to absorption
- 2020MNRAS.498L..87B: Emission unresolved; cannot distinguish envelope from disk; S hot corino needs higher resolution
- 2021A&A...656A..46M: Calibration uncertainty not included in fit uncertainties; line flux scaling anomalies in some tunings
- 2021A&A...656A..46M: STATCONT continuum subtraction not optimal for lines near noise level
- 2020MNRAS.496..394R: Single excitation temperature is a large source of uncertainty.
- 2020MNRAS.496..394R: Spectral index poorly constrained because bands 6 and 7 are adjacent; fluxes and globule mass are lower bounds.
- 2019ApJ...883..180H: Optical depth problem prevents quantitative column density and C/CO abundance derivation
- 2020ApJ...892...99C: Temperature poorly constrained by the data
- 2020ApJ...892...99C: Calibration uncertainty not included in MCMC fit
- 2026A&A...705A.198M: Optically thick masses are lower limits; inner radii are upper limits; degeneracy thick/thin needs radiative transfer
- 2020ApJ...890...95I: Data quality limits accuracy; cannot distinguish UV vs GCR scenarios
- 2013ApJ...776...77K: Inner radius only an upper limit; brightness exponent ill-determined; full radiative transfer model postponed
- 2025MNRAS.541.4031D: Small comparison samples and degeneracy between optical depth and abundance
- 2018MNRAS.475..448T: Distance mismatch between GRS 1915+105 and IRAS source; jet power assumes constant power and density
- 2018MNRAS.475..448T: ALMA continuum lacks single-dish data so flux is underestimated
- 2013A&A...556L...1V: Shell temperature poorly constrained; derived ratios ignore optical depth and chemistry
- 2014ApJ...795...28B: Mass-loss rate is poorly constrained; density is an upper bound, column a lower bound, layer thickness unknown
- 2017ApJ...836..201D: Fiducial model not unique; fitting by eye; overproduces 13CO and C18O outer emission
- 2019ApJ...877L..25M: Beta uncertainty dominates Q; kinematic model not finely fitted; larger-scale envelope resolved out
- 2017ApJ...850...54C: Missing short spacings; about half of expected flux recovered
- 2019A&A...629A.128W: Column densities are lower limits given f_c=1 assumption; G0 underestimated due to extinction
- 2015ApJ...799..204C: Models under-predict HCO+ emission for lines other than (3-2); causes include asymmetry, CO abundance structure and temperature structure
- 2024A&A...686A.201N: Evidence is suggestive; detailed model comparison and alternative entrainment models needed.
- 2024A&A...686A.201N: Disk mass quite uncertain.
- 2014A&A...569A..11S: Extended emission resolved out; H13CO+ linewidths are lower limits; missing flux affects abundances.
- 2025A&A...693A.101T: Radial extent unresolved; beam dilution underestimates column densities
- 2025A&A...693A.101T: Continuum oversubtraction/blocking may reduce line flux
- 2018A&A...615A..28D: Dust masses and dust-to-gas ratios uncertain by about a factor of 5
- 2018A&A...615A..28D: Extended emission may be resolved out
- 2021ApJ...908....8C: Gas mass is valid within the model framework; CO fractionation not included; inclination not explored
- 2016ApJ...821L...8S: Unquantified systematic errors (disc-averaged temperature, Voigt profile, line-broadening coefficients)
- 2015A&A...582L...4M: Metallicity of the foreground galaxy cannot be determined precisely; nucleosynthesis models have uncertain assumptions
- 2020ApJ...891..164S: Infall not detected because no optically thick tracer; NH2 includes low-temperature components
- 2020ApJ...898...75I: Dominance of H2 in the CND is assumed; HI/HII may contribute
- 2020ApJ...898...75I: RADEX assumes single homogeneous medium though real structure is complex; single transition limits Tex
- 2020ApJ...895..119T: ACA missing flux; limited resolution cannot resolve protoplanetary disk; velocity difference near spectral resolution
- 2019ApJ...885L..39H: Southeast positions not definitively detected due to [C I] wing contamination; 12C/13C may exceed 77 so tau is a lower limit
- 2019A&A...629A..75B: Fits are by eye; no main-isotopologue HCN data; low S/N for HC15N
- 2016Natur.540..406B: 6 au resolution cannot exclude an unresolved confined high-velocity component
- 2019A&A...629A...6T: Missing flux, particularly NGC 1068 (~30% 12CN recovered); possible CH3OH blending with 13CN; low 13CN S/N at edges
- 2019A&A...624A..82B: Single CH2NH line blended, giving only upper limits; Tex of CH2NH and NH2CHO unconstrained
- 2019A&A...624A..82B: Models not optimised to NGC 6334 conditions
- 2015ApJ...810..112O: Model is not tuned to IM Lup, so no quantitative comparison is possible
- 2015ApJ...810..112O: Outer-ring intensity is model dependent and may vary from disk to disk
- 2024A&A...691A.180F: Tex fixed to CH3OH value for all species; N_tot uncertain up to factor 2
- 2024A&A...691A.180F: Static models cannot reproduce all ratios; dynamical models needed
- 2013ApJ...770..142N: ALMA data lack zero-spacing; HDO collision rates only up to 450 K so highest HDO lines cannot be modeled; vibrational pumping excluded
- 2024AJ....167...66Y: Emission only marginally resolved; midplane assumption; CH2DOH spectroscopy uncertain by ~factor 3
- 2018A&A...617A..23B: Spherical symmetry assumed despite asymmetric emission
- 2018A&A...617A..23B: Weak lines too low S/N for uv fitting
- 2020MNRAS.493L.108B: Gas mass depends on CO/H2 ratio, possible freeze-out, optical thickness and isotope ratios; precise effects need dedicated modelling.
- 2018ApJ...859L..15C: Ratio not accurate enough to distinguish models; 12C/13C in HC3N uncertain, true ratio could be as low as 43
- 2014A&A...566L...6M: NE covering factor poorly known (0.3<fc<1.0); NE H2(37)Cl+ not detected, only a lower limit on the ratio.
- 2020A&A...637A...7M: Non-simultaneous XD and XH observations and time variability; high uncertainties
- 2020A&A...637A...7M: Assumed covering factor of 1
- 2021A&A...649A.125W: Sensitivity too limited to determine accurate opacity
- 2020A&A...633A.126B: Inclination uncertain; vmax-method momentum force only a lower limit; opacity corrections uncertain
- 2020A&A...633A.126B: Possible contamination from IRS 4 outflow and spatial filtering
- 2019ApJ...882L..31B: Model assumes smooth radial gas density; gas mass is a lower limit due to isotope-selective photodissociation and carbon depletion
- 2017A&A...606L...7B: Higher spatial resolution is needed to distinguish between scenarios; synthetic predictions needed for the disk wind
- 2016AJ....152..218I: Superantennae continuum determination ambiguity larger; HCN v2=1f detection may be contaminated by HCO+ v=0
- 2019A&A...631A..25J: LTE may be invalid if inner envelope densities are lower in isolated sources
- 2013Sci...341..630Q: Vertical disk structure is uncertain; vertical N2H+ boundaries fixed
- 2025A&A...695A.149K: Better angular and spectral resolution needed to confirm Zeeman triplets
- 2025A&A...695A.149K: CH3CN optically thick, so temperatures overestimated
- 2013ApJ...777...85N: NH3 collisional rates used as proxy for NH2D; approximate
- 2024JKAS...57..163L: Simple one-point model; no 2D ring structure or absolute column densities; lines may be optically thick
- 2017A&A...603L...2O: Geometry uncertain; simple model gives only order-of-magnitude abundances
- 2021A&A...651L...6B: Column densities inversely proportional to assumed emitting area, so may be lower limits
- 2017Icar..286..289L: Lower mesosphere and stratopause temperatures are more uncertain, and the HCN vertical distribution is not unique given moderate optical thickness
- 2017Icar..286..289L: Spatial resolution insufficient to resolve surface
- 2019ApJ...883...98Z: Small-scale substructures ignored; smooth density profiles used
- 2019ApJ...883...98Z: Gas-to-dust ratio fixed at 100; gas mass uncertainty considered not crucial
- 2019ApJ...875...62Y: Near systemic velocity emission attenuated/resolved out; observed R13/18 is a lower limit; LTE assumed
- 2017MNRAS.466...49J: 12C/13C ratio uncertain by factor ~2
- 2018A&A...616A..90C: Errors depend on LTE, optically thin and Gaussian assumptions; HC3N only 3 lines, two blended
- 2015ApJ...798...85P: Gas mass is a crude estimate, dominated by assumed isotopic ratios and temperature
- 2025ApJ...985..225L: Scattered light dominates NIR continuum so stellar parameters and radii are underestimated
- 2014ApJ...787..112C: LTE, no radiative pumping, constant source size assumed; some species optically thick
- 2025ApJS..276...49J: Fixed beam-filling factor makes column densities likely lower limits (factor ~2-3)
- 2025ApJS..276...49J: ~20% of lines unidentified
- 2017A&A...599A..63S: Spherical symmetry ignores east-west asymmetry from binary companion
- 2019A&A...632L..12H: Detailed 2D radiative transfer not done; ratio beyond 55 au tentative
- 2017ApJ...843...27L: Tex is poorly constrained because data points are scattered at low S/N; may be underestimated by factor ~2
- 2017ApJ...843...27L: Disk is optically thick in dust so molecules near the midplane cannot be probed
- 2016ApJ...825...44I: Rotational transitions within v=0 and v2=1 not treated; same-region assumption is simplistic
- 2017MNRAS.469.2230M: H2 column is a lower limit, so abundances are upper limits as dust may be optically thick
- 2017MNRAS.469.2230M: NH2CHO underproduced by model by factor 10
- 2013Natur.493..644B: Main uncertainty is the gas temperature structure of the disk
- 2016ApJ...820...19T: Resolution does not allow detailed analysis of ring structures.
- 2016ApJ...827...72S: Trot=100 K assumed for most molecules; SO abundance relies on a single 33SO line; H2CS single low S/N line
- 2018ApJ...856...97S: Column density uncertain by a factor of a few; beam filling factors may differ among tracers
- 2017A&A...605L...6T: Methanol abundances may be overestimated because H2 may be underestimated due to clumpiness and coarse HF resolution
- 2019ApJ...876...72L: Low resolution and S/N cannot distinguish optically thick CS from isotopic enhancement or beam dilution; LTE and filling factor assumptions uncertain
- 2019ApJ...876...72L: Models simplistic: no X-rays, grain growth, LkCa 15 inner cavity; not tuned
- 2019ApJ...872..196S: Rotation temperatures are upper limits and column densities lower limits because low-Eu lines may be optically thick; large uncertainty in 13CH3OH columns; assumed 200 K
- 2017ApJ...840L..11S: C18O may be contaminated by HNCO up to 30%, not corrected
- 2017ApJ...840L..11S: Starburst age and IMF degenerate
- 2017A&A...603L...6H: CN and C15N co-spatiality assumption hard to assess; C15N map not used
- 2017A&A...603L...6H: Robust CN column density needs self-consistent modelling; 2D radiative transfer needed
- 2018ApJ...868...80C: C18O optical depth not derivable in SM1N since C17O covers only 50"x50"
- 2017A&A...606A.109M: Covering factor unresolved; apparent opacities give lower limits for column densities
- 2017A&A...606A.125S: N2D+ is weak, on edge of atmospheric feature, continuum subtraction less accurate
- 2017A&A...606A.125S: Isothermal vertical temperature assumption and no vertical abundance distribution
- 2019ApJ...875...96N: Observation time was ~20% of the requested time, insufficient to test the model

