# Codex review: isotopic-ratios
VERDICT: FIX
## Findings

- SR-01 | medium | attribution | “H13CN/HC15N times 12C/13C = 68 … 2017A&A...603L...6H card” | That paper’s supplied assumption only states HCN/H13CN equals elemental 12C/13C. The pack does not supply 68, UV_FIT, fixed uv geometry, simultaneous-calibration quotation, RADEX agreement within 3% below 20–25 K, scaled hyperfine profiles, or the 0.1-sigma geometry test attributed to it. | Remove these unsupported details; retain the double-isotope conversion with 2020ApJ...898...97B, whose step 7 explicitly supplies 68.
- SR-02 | medium | attribution | “70% … 12CN … 47% … 13CN”; “S/N >~ 5”; “CN is not affected by fractionation” | For 2019A&A...629A...6T, the pack supports LTE, thin 13CN, approximately 30% recovered 12CN in NGC 1068, blending and low edge S/N. It does not supply 47%, the detection threshold, fractionation immunity, CN opacities 0.7–1.1, 13CN hyperfine ratios 1.03–1.25, or the three measured carbon ratios in parameters.md. | Retain supported statements and remove unsupported numbers and methodological claims pending evidence.
- SR-03 | medium | attribution | “0.071 raw and 0.024 … statistically corrected”; “12C/13C … 34” | The supplied pack lists 2018A&A...620A.170J by title but provides neither these results nor their definitions. Calling them “card” does not supply evidence. | Remove these numerical examples or obtain supporting excerpts.
- SR-04 | medium | attribution | “N2D+/N2H+, DCO+/HCO+ … 0.34 … 0.05” | For 2017A&A...606A.125S, the pack supplies temperature choices and lower-limit assumptions, but no numerical deuteration results. | Remove these values; retain the supported temperature brackets and lower-limit qualification.
- SR-05 | medium | attribution | “15 at 69–70”; “3 at 500”; galaxies/LMC “8”; filling/covering “6” | The stated tally rules miss 2015ApJ...810..112O, which adds one paper at both carbon 70 and oxygen 500; 2015ApJ...801...63M adds a ninth galaxy paper at carbon 80. Explicit filling/covering assumptions or constraints occur in at least seven bibcodes, including 2025A&A...695A.149K and 2020A&A...637A...7M. | Correct the first three counts to 16, 4 and 9; provide an enumerated, consistently defined filling/covering tally.
- SR-06 | medium | attribution | “16O/18O … 540 ± 30 … 2015ApJ...799..204C” | The supplied assumption and excerpt explicitly label this **18O/16O**, although that numerical value is physically suspect. The skill silently reverses the label. Its claimed oxygen range also omits the pack’s similarly suspect “16O/18O = 69 ± 11” for 2020A&A...637A...7M. | Mark these as unresolved pack inconsistencies; exclude them explicitly from validated ranges instead of silently correcting or omitting them.
- SR-07 | medium | attribution | “their non-LTE HDO methods are still useful” | This blanket description of the three Herschel papers contradicts the pack’s 2014ApJ...787..112C entry, which states “LTE, no radiative pumping”; 2013ApJ...777...85N instead supplies an NH2D collision-rate limitation. Also, 2013ApJ...770..142N explicitly discusses ALMA zero-spacing limitations. | Describe each supported method separately and avoid categorically excluding ALMA involvement.
- SR-08 | medium | attribution | “Thin pair directly: 13CO/C18O … (2019A&A...624A.125M)” | That paper’s step 5 fits synthetic LTE spectra to obtain column ratios; its limitations explicitly say “13CO moderately optically thick.” The later pitfall does not adequately qualify this recommended route. | Present it as a fitted-column example requiring opacity assessment, rather than an unqualified thin-intensity pair.
- SR-09 | medium | attribution | “CH2DOH, CH2DCN, DC3N D/H … 0.12%, 0.4%, 0.09%” | The 2016A&A...587A..91B excerpts report molecular deuteration levels and describe XD/XH; they do not establish statistically corrected atomic D/H for those numbers. | Preserve the reported molecular-ratio definitions and distinguish them from site-corrected D/H.
- SR-10 | high | science | “I_main/I_rare = (1 − exp(−tau_main))/(1 − exp(−tau_rare))” | Equal Tex and filling alone do not make this exact for arbitrary intensities or different frequencies. Moreover, the workflow primarily measures integrated intensities, whereas this relation describes corresponding spectral brightnesses; integrating profiles does not generally preserve the scalar relation. The pack’s 2020MNRAS.496..394R method explicitly works per pixel, per channel. | Define brightness units, include the frequency-dependent source-function/background factors, and solve per channel or fit integrated radiative-transfer profiles. State the assumptions behind tau_main = X tau_rare and the thick-main approximation.
- SR-11 | medium | science | “Double isotope … 13CO/13C18O”; “Hyperfine self-calibration … [CI]/[13CI]” | 13CO/13C18O directly probes oxygen substitution under the stated chemistry assumptions; it needs no carbon multiplier. Conversely, the [CI] opacity estimate explicitly assumes 12C/13C = 77 in 2019ApJ...885L..39H and is not isotope-independent self-calibration. Also, 13CO/C18O combines carbon and oxygen ratios. | Separate these routes and give the algebra: N(13CO)/N(C18O) ≈ (16O/18O)/(12C/13C); distinguish CN hyperfine opacity from isotope-assumed [CI] opacity.
- SR-12 | medium | science | “The flux-calibration error cancels only if both lines share a spectral window or execution; otherwise add it” | Sharing an execution or spectral window does not guarantee complete cancellation, and separate observations need not have independent calibration errors. The pack flags calibration exclusions and tuning-dependent scaling anomalies in 2021A&A...656A..46M. | Propagate calibration covariance; claim cancellation only for demonstrated common multiplicative errors, while retaining differential calibration uncertainty.
- SR-13 | medium | omission | “one mask … above 3 sigma in both” | This reproduces 2020ApJ...898...97B, but prescribing it without a selection-bias check can bias weak-line ratios. There is also no actionable nondetection branch, despite explicit ratio lower limits in 2014A&A...566L...6M and deuteration upper limits in 2016A&A...587A..91B. | Identify the mask as a literature example; test clipping sensitivity and specify confidence levels and correct ratio-bound directions for nondetections.
- SR-14 | medium | omission | “continuum level matters” | The skill discusses baseline subtraction but omits physical dust blocking and line suppression: 2025A&A...693A.101T flags continuum oversubtraction/blocking, and 2017ApJ...843...27L says optically thick dust hides midplane molecules. These can defeat otherwise matched isotopologue comparisons. | Add a dust-opacity and continuum-blocking check before interpreting line deficits or ratios.
- SR-15 | medium | omission | “correct … Einstein A, frequency, partition function and lower-level energy” | The cited 2018A&A...615A..28D method additionally requires matching quantum numbers and no differential radiative pumping. Those conditions are missing from the operational instruction. | Require matched transitions and assess differential pumping; route unsuitable pairs to excitation/radiative-transfer modelling.

## Notes
The skill captures many important limitations and reproduces most supplied software counts accurately.
The main provenance problem is extensive reliance on “card” details absent from this evidence pack.
Keep reported molecular ratios, corrected D/H, assumed elemental inputs and derived opacities explicitly distinct.
